; digest: a daily brief of this repository, from an agent that reads it
; with whiff's functions. Once a day it looks at the open pull requests and
; their checks, the open items in TODO.md and the uncommitted work, and
; leaves a short brief in your inbox: what changed since the last one, or
; nothing at all if nothing did. Ask it any time for one, or a question:
;   whiff call digest/ask "brief me"   ; pending; whiff wait <id>
;   whiff call digest/tell "what's blocking the release?"   ; answer in your inbox
;
; Its tools are :read, so its turns never wait on you. :dir ".." is this
; repository, from the file's real place: link it into ~/.whiff/services,
; or copy it with :dir set to another project. Every 1d counts from when
; whiff starts. Needs the claude and gh CLIs.

(agent digest
  :prompt """
    You keep the user's daily brief of the repository your tools act in.
    Look with them: gh_prs and gh_checks for pull requests and their checks,
    todo_open for what is open in TODO.md, git_status for the branch and
    uncommitted work. Then write at most eight lines: what changed since
    your last brief first (a check that started failing, a new pull
    request, items done or added, work left uncommitted), then anything
    that needs the user today. Name pull requests by number and TODO items
    by their text. Don't repeat what you said last time unless it still
    needs them. TODO.md is the user's local roadmap, uncommitted on
    purpose: don't count it as uncommitted work.
    """
  :can [:gh/prs :gh/checks :todo/open :git/status]
  :dir ".."
  :every 1d)
